cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EvergreenSLAM in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EvergreenSLAM: always-on 2D lidar SLAM as the long-term spatial memory of an agent"
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Hang
    email: chen@hang.plus
repository-code: "https://github.com/ThomasZB/EvergreenSLAM"
url: "https://github.com/ThomasZB/EvergreenSLAM"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3-preview
date-released: 2026-10-16
abstract: >-
  Always-on, hands-off, agent-friendly 2D lidar SLAM. Maps are created, frozen and
  extended automatically across power cycles, with pose-graph trimming by
  marginalization and Chow-Liu sparsification to keep the graph bounded. Named places
  (anchors) bind to graph nodes rather than coordinates, and an agent reads and writes
  its spatial memory as plain files through a CLI and an MCP server.
keywords:
  - slam
  - 2d-slam
  - lidar
  - lifelong-slam
  - pose-graph
  - spatial-memory
  - embodied-ai
  - llm-agents
  - mcp
  - ros2
  - robotics
